Today parseItemSpec (src/commands.ts:181) and config install lists accept only name@source / type:name@source. Wanted: a wildcard per type and source, e.g. "rules": ["*@shared"] in config and `skilletor install 'rule:*@shared'`, so a source can ship a rule set that is installed as a whole.

Design points to settle (spec §3/§4 update first):
- Expansion happens at sync time against the source catalog, so items added upstream arrive automatically and items removed upstream are deleted via the lock (same as today's undeclared-item removal).
- Explicit entries and wildcard overlap: explicit wins / dedupe; name collisions across two wildcards of the same type and scope stay a config error (§3 duplicate rule).
- Trust unchanged: wildcard only over trusted sources; project-declared wildcard on an untrusted source reports like today.
- Scope: all three types or rules only? Proposal: all types, since the catalog is per type anyway.
- status/available should show which installed items came from a wildcard.
Target: skilletor-worker (engine, tests, dist) + skilletor-skill-author for SKILL.md/README docs.

